4
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:10,530
controlled problem, repairs it, and proves

5
00:00:10,530 --> 00:00:11,350
the result.

6
00:00:12,286 --> 00:00:14,286
Here is one React checkout journey.

7
00:00:15,086 --> 00:00:17,983
I use only the keyboard to add the sample

8
00:00:17,983 --> 00:00:19,593
product, open checkout, enter synthetic

9
00:00:19,593 --> 00:00:21,846
data, and move to the primary action.

10
00:00:22,366 --> 00:00:25,166
The email field shows visible text, but

11
00:00:25,166 --> 00:00:27,166
it has no programmatically associated

12
00:00:27,166 --> 00:00:29,696
accessible name. The primary action

13
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:32,116
receives keyboard focus, but no visible

14
00:00:32,116 --> 00:00:33,326
focus cue appears.

15
00:00:34,094 --> 00:00:36,334
The form still reaches confirmation.

16
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:39,494
AccessPatch records barriers in the real

17
00:00:39,494 --> 00:00:41,688
journey state, not only in isolated

18
00:00:41,688 --> 00:00:42,054
components.

19
00:00:42,878 --> 00:00:45,838
The evidence contains exactly two findings.

20
00:00:46,758 --> 00:00:49,434
Axe reports one label violation on the

21
00:00:49,434 --> 00:00:52,186
email field. Browser evidence records

22
00:00:52,186 --> 00:00:55,140
no visible outline or box shadow on the

23
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:55,878
focused button.

24
00:00:56,838 --> 00:00:59,515
One bounded GPT-5.6 call reviewed

25
00:00:59,515 --> 00:01:02,192
this evidence, with store set to

26
00:01:02,192 --> 00:01:05,168
false. It used 2,444

27
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:07,918
recorded tokens and selected two

28
00:01:07,918 --> 00:01:10,118
allowlisted repair strategies.

29
00:01:11,038 --> 00:01:13,776
It did not write or directly apply source

30
00:01:13,776 --> 00:01:15,110
code.

31
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:18,400
Deterministic templates perform the repair

32
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,950
